    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Let me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added weekly subscription support to subtrack. Here's what was implemented:\n\n### Core Changes\n\n1. **src/cycles.js** - Added weekly billing cycle support:\n   - Added `CYCLE.WEEK: 'weekly'` to cycle definitions\n   - Set `MONTHS_PER_CHARGE[CYCLE.WEEK] = 12 / 52` (weekly charges cover 12/52 months)\n   - Updated `nextCharge()` to calculate charges every 7 days from the `--since` date\n\n2. **bin/subtrack.js** - CLI support for weekly:\n   - Updated usage to show `--every week|month|year`\n   - Added 'week' and 'weekly' to the EVERY mapping\n   - Added `SHARE_PER_MONTH[CYCLE.WEEK] = 52 / 12` for cost calculations\n\n3. **src/export.js** - CSV export support:\n   - Added weekly to the MONTHS constant\n\n4. **src/renewals.js** - Fixed renewal sorting:\n   - Fixed a bug where renewals were sorted by label string instead of days until renewal\n\n### Testing\n\nAdded comprehensive test coverage:\n- Weekly plan cost calculations (price \u00d7 52 \u00f7 12)\n- Weekly charge scheduling (every 7 days)\n- CLI integration tests\n- CSV export tests\n\n### Documentation\n\nUpdated README.md with:\n- Weekly plan examples\n- Updated options table\n- Money calculation formulas\n\n**All 41 tests pass.** The feature works as specified:\n- `subtrack add \"Meal kit\" 59.90 --every week` creates a weekly plan\n- A \u20ac12 weekly plan shows as \u20ac52.00/month\n- Weekly charges appear in `subtrack renewals` like any other plan",
